        "slide": 3,
        "role": "evidence",
        "subject": "A graphite carrier plate seen in plan. It holds an 8 by 8 block of brushed steel tray fronts and, across a wide groove, one row of eight black anodised tray fronts with lit cyan strips. Every tray is the same 86 by 42 unit envelope, with a lid seam, a perforated bezel band, two handle ears and a chamfer lit on its upper and left edges, casting to the lower right into its gutter.",
        "visual_consequence": "Eight full rows of grey trays stand against one row of cyan trays of the same width and tray size, so the eight to one count reads as area at 432 px before the headline does. Cyan marks the Vista group only, and nothing draws a speed, a bar or an axis.",
        "weakness": "Re-read after a FIG-line-only change on a byte-identical render (sha256 31676624f191...). The dek's last line almost touches the carrier's top rim; casts on the right column and below the black row run past the carrier's edge as a stepped fringe; the black lids sit close in value to the graphite carrier, so the row is carried by its strips, chamfers and ears.",
        "repair": "None required for acceptance. If the frame is touched again, move Y0 down about 10 design px so the dek clears the rim.",
